      "statement": "Smallness, typing, separate naming or independent testability of a file, function, class, record, operation, diagram, module or owner category does not establish Prime. Atomic-function Prime requires complete-family contraction. Every accepted atom declares its admitted domain and governs every admitted instance in it. Later uses compose or parameterise it without local fork, shadow, specialisation or reinterpretation. An out-of-domain case may motivate another candidate for admission; an in-domain counterexample falsifies the shared atom and re-enters its design boundary, not a feature-local replacement. An undeclared domain leaves candidate status and supplies neither Prime acceptance nor projection Prime-conformance.",
